---
title: James J Nadeau | Growing Our Officials
description: "How many northern Vermont football officials we need to end Thursday games and keep everyone to one game a weekend."
---

//- Rows run left to right, then right to left, one row per section.
- var xspace = 1500;
- var yspace = 1200;

#impress
  //- Section 1: where we are
  #title.step(data-x=0 data-y=0)
    h1 🏈 How Many Officials Do We Need?
    p.lead Growing our northern football crew
    p 📊 Using Arbiter game data from 2023 to 2026
    .notes.
      All numbers come from the Arbiter assignment data, through mid-October 2026.
      "Northern" means games at fields north of the gap between Otter Valley and Middlebury.
      "Varsity" means Varsity, Varsity Coed, and state playoff games. JV is left out.

  #goals.step(data-x=1*xspace data-y=0)
    h1 🎯 Our Two Goals
    ol
      li.substep 🚫 No more Thursday night games
      li.substep ☝️ Each official works only one varsity game a weekend
    p.substep 🤔 How many officials do we need for each goal?

  #today.step(data-x=2*xspace data-y=0)
    h1 📋 Where We Are Now
    ul
      li 👥 41 northern officials worked varsity in 2026
      li 🏈 76 varsity games in 10 weeks
      li 🦓 Each game needs 5 officials
      li 📅 Almost all games are on Friday or Saturday

  #trend.step(data-x=3*xspace data-y=0)
    h2 📉 Officials Each Year
    img.img-fluid(src="/files/officials-growth/officials-by-year.svg" alt="Bar chart of varsity officials each year. North: 38, 37, 36, 41. South: 26, 25, 23, 21.")
    p The north grew this year. The south keeps getting smaller.

  //- Section 2: goal 1, right to left
  #thursday.step(data-x=3*xspace data-y=1*yspace)
    h2 🗓️ Goal 1: How Many Thursday Games?
    img.img-fluid(src="/files/officials-growth/thursday-games.svg" alt="Bar chart of northern Thursday varsity games each year: 7, 7, 4, 6.")
    p We play 4 to 7 Thursday games a year. Most weeks have none.

  #move.step(data-x=2*xspace data-y=1*yspace)
    h2 🔀 Move Thursday to Friday
    img.img-fluid(src="/files/officials-growth/friday-if-moved.svg" alt="Stacked bar chart of officials needed each Friday in 2026 if Thursday games move to Friday. Two Fridays reach 35.")
    p Two Fridays would need 35 officials.

  #goal1-table.step(data-x=1*xspace data-y=1*yspace)
    h2 📊 Weeks With Thursday Games (2026)
    table.table.table-striped(style="font-size:1.4rem")
      thead
        tr
          th Weekend
          th Friday now
          th From Thu
          th Total
      tbody
        tr
          td Sep 4
          td 20
          td 5
          td 25
        tr
          td Sep 11
          td 5
          td 10
          td 15
        tr
          td Oct 9
          td 25
          td 5
          td 30
        tr
          td Oct 16
          td 25
          td 10
          td
            strong 35
    p Our busiest Friday this year already needed 35 (Sep 25).

  #goal1-answer.step(data-x=0 data-y=1*yspace)
    h1 ✅ Goal 1 Answer
    p.substep 🦓 The busiest Friday needs 35 officials.
    p.substep 🙋 Not everyone is free every week.
    p.substep 🔢 If 8 out of 10 are free, we need 44.
    p.substep.lead 💪 We have 41. We need 3 more.
    .notes.
      On Sep 25 we needed 35 officials. We got there by borrowing 4 from the south.
      "8 out of 10 free" is a guess, not a measured number.

  //- Section 3: goal 2, left to right
  #doubles.step(data-x=0 data-y=2*yspace)
    h2 🔁 Goal 2: Many Officials Work Twice
    img.img-fluid(src="/files/officials-growth/doubles.svg" alt="Bar chart of officials working two varsity games in one weekend in 2026. Most weekends 7 to 16, highest 19 on Sep 25.")
    p Most weekends, about 11 officials work 2 varsity games.

  #spots.step(data-x=1*xspace data-y=2*yspace)
    h2 🦓 Spots to Fill Each Weekend
    img.img-fluid(src="/files/officials-growth/weekly-spots.svg" alt="Bar chart of varsity spots each weekend in 2026, from 20 to 55, with a line at 41 officials.")
    p On 3 weekends, we had more spots than officials!

  #goal2-table.step(data-x=2*xspace data-y=2*yspace)
    h2 📊 One Game Each: How Many?
    table.table.table-striped(style="font-size:1.4rem")
      thead
        tr
          th Weekend
          th Spots
          th We need *
          th More
      tbody
        tr
          td 😌 Easy
          td 35
          td 44
          td +3
        tr
          td 🙂 Normal
          td 40
          td 50
          td +9
        tr
          td 😅 Busy
          td 45
          td 57
          td +16
        tr
          td 😰 Busiest
          td 55
          td
            strong 69
          td
            strong +28
    p
      small * If 8 out of 10 officials are free that weekend.

  #goal2-answer.step(data-x=3*xspace data-y=2*yspace)
    h1 ✅ Goal 2 Answer
    p.substep 👥 We need about 69 officials.
    p.substep ➕ That is 28 more than we have now.
    p.substep.lead 🎉 Good news: this fixes Goal 1 too!
    .notes.
      With 69 officials, a 35-person Friday is easy to cover.
      So if we reach Goal 2, we also reach Goal 1.

  //- Section 4: growing, right to left
  #come-go.step(data-x=3*xspace data-y=3*yspace)
    h2 🚪 Officials Come and Go
    table.table.table-striped(style="font-size:1.4rem")
      thead
        tr
          th Season
          th Stopped 👋
          th Started 🆕
      tbody
        tr
          td 2024
          td 7
          td 6
        tr
          td 2025
          td 4
          td 2
        tr
          td 2026
          td 2
          td 7
    p About 1 in 8 officials stop each year. About 5 new ones start. So we stay about the same size.
    .notes.
      "Stopped" means they worked varsity one year and not the next.
      Over three years, 13 of 111 stopped. That is about 12 percent, or 1 in 8.

  #growth-chart.step(data-x=2*xspace data-y=3*yspace)
    h2 📈 How Fast Can We Grow?
    img.img-fluid(src="/files/officials-growth/growth.svg" alt="Line chart from 2026 to 2032 for 5, 10, 15 and 20 new officials a year, with goal lines at 44 and 69.")
    p Each line is a different number of new officials each year.

  #growth-table.step(data-x=1*xspace data-y=3*yspace)
    h2 📊 When Do We Reach Our Goals?
    table.table.table-striped(style="font-size:1.4rem")
      thead
        tr
          th New each year
          th Goal 1 (44)
          th Goal 2 (69)
      tbody
        tr
          td 5 (like now)
          td Never
          td Never
        tr
          td 10
          td 2027
          td 2035
        tr
          td 15
          td 2027
          td 2030
        tr
          td 20
          td 2027
          td 2028
    p.lead We need 15 to 20 new officials each year.
    .notes.
      This assumes about 1 in 8 officials stop each year, like the last three years.
      More officials means more people stopping too, so growth slows down over time.

  #south.step(data-x=0 data-y=3*yspace)
    h2 🧭 What About the South?
    ul
      li 👥 21 varsity officials now (26 in 2023)
      li 🆕 Only 1 new varsity official this year
      li 🤝 They helped us on Sep 25 with 4 officials
      li ⚠️ They cannot fill our gap. They need to grow too.

  //- Section 5: wrap up, left to right
  #keep-in-mind.step(data-x=0 data-y=4*yspace)
    h2 ⚠️ Things to Keep in Mind
    ul
      li 🔢 "8 out of 10 free" is a guess. Let's ask our officials!
      li 🎓 New officials often start with JV games first
      li 🏟️ Some Thursday games may be there for a reason, like lights or fields
      li 🧮 Our numbers are small. One person can change a lot.

  #summary.step(data-x=1*xspace data-y=4*yspace)
    h1 🏁 What We Need
    table.table.table-striped(style="font-size:1.4rem")
      thead
        tr
          th Goal
          th Officials
          th More
      tbody
        tr
          td 🚫 No Thursdays
          td 44
          td +3
        tr
          td ☝️ One game each
          td 69
          td +28
    p.lead 🌱 To get there: 15 to 20 new officials a year.

  #end.step(data-x=2*xspace data-y=4*yspace)
    h1 🙋 Questions?
    p Thank you!

  //- Centre of the 4 x 5 grid: x 0..4500, y 0..4800.
  #overview.step(data-x=1.5*xspace data-y=2*yspace data-scale=6)
